---
title: Native foreground publisher shutdown
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> ready
    ready --> enrolled : Interrupt
    ready --> enrolled : FrontendLost [lifetime watch]
    ready --> publisher_down : PublisherCrash [exact Child reaped]
    publisher_down --> enrolled : Interrupt or SIGHUP
    publisher_down --> enrolled : FrontendLost [lifetime watch]
    publisher_down --> intent : Recover [owner absent]
    state "publisher-down" as publisher_down
    note left of publisher_down
        Exit reported; published port down
        Services stay running and observable
        Run hack down for confirmed cleanup
    end note
    enrolled --> enrolled : StopPublisher
    ready --> intent : Recover [owner absent]
    enrolled --> intent : Recover [owner absent]
    intent --> intent : StopPublisher [identity matches]
    enrolled --> bridge_retired : ReleaseBridge [publisher absent]
    intent --> bridge_retired : ReleaseBridge [proof current]
    bridge_retired --> intent : Recover [owner absent]
    bridge_retired --> stopped : CleanupGuest [proof current]
    stopped --> stopped : ReleaseDependencies [proof current]
    stopped --> retired : Retire [no reservation]
    retired --> [*]
    state "bridge-retired" as bridge_retired
    note right of intent
        Dead owner and pinned coordinator
        Same or audited successor boot
        Exact bridge and environment inventory
        Changed evidence retains this intent
    end note
    note right of bridge_retired
        Publisher and bridge helper absent
        Capacity released before compute removal
    end note
    note right of retired
        Compute absent, data retained
        Foreground publication retired
        Dependency reservations absent
        Dead frontend finalization recovered by down --recover
    end note
    note left of stopped
        Guest completion can precede reservation release
        Retirement retries release under the same proofs
    end note
